340	SG	Universal Surface Gauge	Universal Surface Gauge	Precision_Catalogue_CA_03	36	vision_pipeline/data/Precision_Catalogue_CA_03/chunks/0044_sg.md	# Universal Surface Gauge\n\n**Product Code:** `SG`\n**Category:** Universal Surface Gauge\n**Source Page:** 36\n\n## Description\n\nThe Universal Surface Gauge is used for scribing lines transferring measurements probing surfaces in inspection. Fully hardened and ground base serves as an accurate reference surface. Machined Vee groove in the base allows the gauge to be used conveniently on curved surfaces. Vee groove at the front end allows the spindle to adjust to any angle above or below the base allowing it to be used as a height or depth gauge. Two retractable pins allow the gauge to be located against the edge of a surface plate or T-slot for linear work. 1/4" (6.35 mm) hole in the spring loaded scriber holder allows a dial indicator to be attached conveniently making the gauge useful for checking flatness, parallelism, heights, depths etc. Grooves on the side of the base allow for comfortable grip. Well tapered scriber for better sighting while working. The scriber tip is hardened to 55-60 HRC\n\n## Features\n\n- Fully hardened and ground base\n- Machined Vee groove in the base\n- Vee groove at the front end\n- Two retractable pins\n- 1/4" (6.35 mm) hole in the spring loaded scriber holder\n- Grooves on the side of the base\n- Well tapered scriber tip hardened to 55-60 HRC\n\n## Utility\n\n- Scribing lines\n- Transferring measurements\n- Probing surfaces\n- Checking flatness\n- Checking parallelism\n- Checking heights\n- Checking depths\n\n## Specifications\n\n- **other:** 1/4" (6.35 mm) hole for dial indicator\n\n## Variants\n\n### SG/9-12\n\n**Universal Surface Gauge**\n\nSurface Gauge being used to scribe a horizontal line parallel to the ground, on a work piece\n\n#### Specifications\n\n- **other:** 12" (300 mm) with extra 9" (225 mm) spindle\n\n#### Ordering Information\n\n| Cat_No | Ord_No | Size | Weight | Box_Qty | EAN | Price |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| SG/9-12 | 03201 | 3-1/8 x 2-1/2 (80 x 63) | None | 15 | None | None |\n\n---\n	{"Utility": "- Scribing lines\\n- Transferring measurements\\n- Probing surfaces\\n- Checking flatness\\n- Checking parallelism\\n- Checking heights\\n- Checking depths", "Features": "- Fully hardened and ground base\\n- Machined Vee groove in the base\\n- Vee groove at the front end\\n- Two retractable pins\\n- 1/4\\" (6.35 mm) hole in the spring loaded scriber holder\\n- Grooves on the side of the base\\n- Well tapered scriber tip hardened to 55-60 HRC", "Variants": "### SG/9-12\\n\\n**Universal Surface Gauge**\\n\\nSurface Gauge being used to scribe a horizontal line parallel to the ground, on a work piece\\n\\n#### Specifications\\n\\n- **other:** 12\\" (300 mm) with extra 9\\" (225 mm) spindle\\n\\n#### Ordering Information\\n\\n| Cat_No | Ord_No | Size | Weight | Box_Qty | EAN | Price |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| SG/9-12 | 03201 | 3-1/8 x 2-1/2 (80 x 63) | None | 15 | None | None |\\n\\n---", "Description": "The Universal Surface Gauge is used for scribing lines transferring measurements probing surfaces in inspection. Fully hardened and ground base serves as an accurate reference surface. Machined Vee groove in the base allows the gauge to be used conveniently on curved surfaces. Vee groove at the front end allows the spindle to adjust to any angle above or below the base allowing it to be used as a height or depth gauge. Two retractable pins allow the gauge to be located against the edge of a surface plate or T-slot for linear work. 1/4\\" (6.35 mm) hole in the spring loaded scriber holder allows a dial indicator to be attached conveniently making the gauge useful for checking flatness, parallelism, heights, depths etc. Grooves on the side of the base allow for comfortable grip. Well tapered scriber for better sighting while working. The scriber tip is hardened to 55-60 HRC", "Specifica